          "rag_type": "graph",
          "correct": true,
          "f1": 0.9,
          "latency_ms": 12518,
          "answer": "The object in question is the Sun. The reference context explains that planetary geologists struggled for a long time to measure its oxygen isotope ratios, with the breakthrough coming from the Genesis spacecraft's silicon wafer analysis. Separately, the context notes that heliocentrism—the model placing the Sun at the center of the Solar System—was proposed as early as the 3rd century BC by Aristarchus of Samos. Since the Sun's central position was established long before its oxygen composition",
