          "id": "graph-musique-20",
          "rag_type": "graph",
          "correct": false,
          "f1": 0.0571,
          "latency_ms": 11258,
          "answer": "Kepler's laws describe planetary motion with the Sun at the center, so the key is identifying when that was established. The laws themselves were published in the early 17th century, but they built on earlier work. Copernicus had already proposed a heliocentric model in the mid-1500s, and Galileo's telescopic observations in the early 1600s provided strong observational support. By the time Kepler formulated his laws, the idea that the Sun was the center of the solar system was already widely ac",
          "expected": "as early as the 3rd century BC",
          "match_type": "TOKEN_F1",
